From 8dfb8999211259c0632a3727deb09961e28718e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:54:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 08/17] feat(mcp): carry the failing field's schema in call
 validation errors

Info and schema drill-downs were 57% of response tokens in the friction
session, mostly mandated by the "SCHEMA DRILL-DOWN RULE - HARD
REQUIREMENT". The server's own validation errors already name the field
(P9, #139/#140), but not its shape, so a caller still had to drill.

A call that fails validation now returns, under the usual message, the
summarized schema of each failing field (up to three, deduplicated by
shape), using schema-utils' summarizeSchema unchanged. A missing or
mistyped scalar is shown through its parent object, so its siblings and
enum values are visible; a length rejection, which already names the
bound, carries none. The text is capped at 8,000 characters and comes
from the tool schema only, never from caller input; analytics keeps the
short message.

The drill-down rule is softened to "look up the schema if a call fails or
the shape is unfamiliar", and the "run info for ALL tools first" line is
gone. info and schema work as before; the JSON Schema they show now comes
from one cached helper.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
